cific tool you'll use\n30: 3. For NexLev: the daily limit and how many calls remain in this session\n31: \n32: Then proceed. vidIQ calls don't need usage tracking — user manages credits.\n33: \n34: ---\n35: \n36: ## ROUTING DECISION TREE\n37: \n38: ### Step 1: Is This NexLev-Exclusive?\n39: \n40: If the task requires ANY of these, you MUST use NexLev — vidIQ cannot do them:\n41: \n42: | Category | NexLev Tools | Daily Cap |\n43: |---|---|---|\n44: | **Monetization check** | `check_channel_monetization`, `check_video_monetization` | 5 each |\n45: | **Faceless detection** | `check_faceless_channel`, `latest_discovered_faceless_niches`, `faceless_outliers_videos` | 5, 20, 20 |\n46: | **Niche finder** | `search_niche_finder_channels`, `get_niche_overview`, `get_niche_finder_categories`, `get_niche_finder_formats`, `get_niche_finder_tags` | 10, 5, 10, 10, 5 |\n47: | **Sponsorship/promotions** | `get_channel_promotions`, `get_channel_promotions_realtime` | 5, 2 |\n48: | **Viral small channels** | `search_viral_videos_small_channels` | 20 |\n49: | **RPM & geo revenue** | `get_video_rpm`, `get_geography_revenue` | 5 each |\n50: | **Shorts vs long split** | `get_short_vs_long_views` | 5 |\n51: | **Daily analytics** | `get_daily_analytics` | 5 |\n52: | **Bulk operations** | `get_batch_channel_metrics`, `get_bulk_video_transcripts`, `get_bulk_video_subtitles`, `get_video_subtitle` | 5 each |\n53: | **Find channel types** | `find_long_form_channels`, `find_shorts_channels` | 10 each |\n54: | **Suggested videos** | `search_youtube_suggested_videos` | 20 |\n55: | **Channel resolver** | `channel_resolver` (handle → ID) | 10 |\n56: | **Watch TikTok/IG video** | `watch_tiktok_video_and_ask`, `watch_instagram_video_and_ask` | 1 each |\n57: \n58: → If YES: Use NexLev. Report the tool, its daily cap, and session usage.\n59: \n60: ### Step 2: Is This vidIQ-Exclusive?\n61: \n62: If the task requires ANY of these, you MUST use vidIQ — NexLev cannot do them:\n63: \n64: | Category | vidIQ Tools |\n65: |---|---|\n66: | **AI content generation** | `generate_titles`, `generate_script`, `generate_video`, `generate_broll`, `generate_music`, `generate_clips`, `generate_thumbnail`, `refine_thumbnail`, `generate_comment_replies`, `compose`, `motion_graphics`, `edit_media` |\n67: | **Voiceover** | `voiceover_list_voices`, `voiceover_generate`, `voiceover_clone`, `voiceover_clone_start` |\n68: | **SEO & scoring** | `keyword_research`, `score_title`, `score_thumbnail` |\n69: | **Analytics & insights** | `subscriber_insights`, `channel_performance_trends`, `video_change_history`, `trend_categories` |\n70: | **IG/TikTok research** | `ig_profile`, `ig_profile_reels`, `instagram_tiktok_outlier_search`, `ig_accounts_from_outliers`, `watch_shortform_content` |\n71: | **Competitor tracking** | `list_competitors`, `update_competitors` |\n72: | **Earnings estimate** | `video_earnings_estimate`, `earnings_calculate` |\n73: \n74: → If YES: Use vidIQ. No usage tracking needed.\n75: \n76: ### Step 3: Both Can Do It?\n77: \n78: For overlapping capabilities, **ALWAYS use vidIQ** (unlimited credits):\n79: \n80: | Task | Use vidIQ | NOT NexLev |\n81: |---|---|---|\n82: | YouTube search | `youtube_search` | ~~youtube_search~~ |\n83: | Channel stats | `channel_stats` | ~~youtube_channel_about~~ |\n84: | Channel videos | `channel_videos` | ~~youtube_channel_videos~~ |\n85: | Video stats | `video_stats` | ~~youtube_video_details~~ |\n86: | Video comments | `video_comments` | ~~youtube_video_comments~~ |\n87: | Video transcript | `video_transcript` | ~~get_video_transcript~~ |\n88: | Similar channels | `similar_channels` | ~~get_similar_channels~~ |\n89: | Similar videos | `similar_videos` | ~~get_similar_videos~~ |\n90: | Similar thumbnails | `similar_thumbnails` | ~~get_similar_thumbnails~~ |\n91: | Outlier videos | `outliers` | ~~youtube_channel_outliers~~ |\n92: | Channel analytics | `channel_analytics` | ~~get_channel_analytics~~ |\n93: | Watch YouTube video | `video_watch` | ~~