{"step_index":20,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-20T08:34:59Z","content":"Priyanshu, understood — you don't want me to do the research. You want me to review your prompt and give you a clean, optimized version to paste into vidIQ AI Coach. Let me do that.","thinking":"Let me understand what Priyanshu is asking:\n\n1. He wants to evaluate the audiobook/book summary niche on YouTube\n2. He's found several channels that motivated him and wants to understand if they're monetized, how they're performing, etc.\n3. He's created a prompt that he wants to paste somewhere (likely into vidIQ AI Coach or a similar tool) to get data-backed analysis\n4. He wants me to review his prompt and either approve it or customize it\n5. He does NOT want me to do the research myself — he wants a ready-to-paste prompt\n\nKey things he mentioned:\n- He has NexLev extension to check monetization\n- He wants a prompt tight enough to avoid hallucinations, and he's specifically curious why English Avenuee isn't demonetized despite looking like typical AI content\n\nHe listed the channels inspiring him: SoulArcStudios, LifeUpgrade27, AudiobooksArc, SwaroopSinghRajput, Antidote_thechannel, Elite_Audiobooks, EnglishAvenuee. I should check the vidiq-nexlev-router and vidiq-youtube-creator skills to see what tools are available before structuring my response.\n\nHe explicitly said not to do the full research job — just review his existing prompt, refine it, and make it paste-ready for vidIQ AI Coach, keeping it concise. His draft is solid but has an inconsistency between \"95% AI content\" and \"~90%\" that I should fix, plus it needs to cover viability, monetization risk, RPM, copyright, and Hindi vs English clearly without bloating the length.\n\nHe also wants NexLev mentioned for monetization checks and real channel data included, so the plan is to review his draft, tighten it into a concise prompt with channel URLs, NexLev capability, and monetization context, keeping in mind vidIQ AI Coach works best with focused rather than sprawling multi-part queries.\n\nSplitting into focused prompts seems better given vidIQ AI Coach works best with narrower queries and less hallucination risk. But Priyanshu made clear he doesn't want me doing the research myself — he just wants his existing prompt reviewed and optimized for pasting. I'll skip the skill files and just work with what I know: fixing his inconsistent stats (95% vs ~90% AI content) and untangling the bundled questions that might confuse the tool.\n\nActually vidIQ AI Coach handles strategy and risk discussions too, so one comprehensive prompt could work if structured well. I'll review his original prompt briefly, fix the inconsistencies (90% vs 95%, missing channel URLs, no NexLev mention, weak closing line), and produce a cleaner optimized version with a breakdown of what each section does.\n\nHis current prompt is about 250 words, which is a fine length for vidIQ AI Coach — I'll keep my version similar. Time to write it up.","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Review of Priyanshu's audiobook niche evaluation prompt, with a customized optimized version ready to paste into vidIQ AI Coach. Includes line-by-line breakdown of what each part does and why, plus notes on what vidIQ CAN vs CANNOT answer.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Audiobook Niche Prompt — Review & Optimized Version\n\n---\n\n## Your Original Prompt — What's Good & What's Wrong\n\n### ✅ What's working\n- The 5-question structure is solid — gives the AI clear deliverables\n- Your plan section (content type, length, AI usage, monetization) is great context\n- Asking for \"no fluff, no motivation\" sets the right tone\n\n### ❌ What needs fixing\n\n| Problem | Where | Fix |\n|---------|-------|-----|\n| **90% vs 95% contradiction** | Plan says \"~90%\", Question 2 says \"95%\" | Pick one. 90% is more accurate since you're doing manual script QC |\n| **Channel URLs missing** | End of prompt says \"analyze their performance\" but no URLs | Must include them or vidIQ has nothing to analyze |\n| **No NexLev mention** | You have NexLev to verify monetization — prompt doesn't tell the AI this | Add it so the AI gives you checkable claims |\n| **Copyright question is wasted** | vidIQ is a keyword/analytics tool — it doesn't know copyright law well | I'll keep it but reframe it toward what vidIQ CAN answer (which channels got hit, not legal advice) |\n| **\"Analyze if you can\" is weak** | Last line is vague — AI will half-ass it | Rewrite with specific asks per channel |\n| **Typos and grammar** | Multiple spots | Cleaned up — AI performs worse with messy input |\n| **Too many sub-questions per section** | Some sections have 3-4 nested questions | Tightened so AI doesn't skip any |\n\n---\n\n## Optimized Prompt — Ready to Paste\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Copy everything inside the code block below. Paste directly into vidIQ AI Coach.\n\n```\nI'm evaluating the YouTube audiobook/book summary niche before starting a channel. Give me a data-backed honest assessment — no fluff, no motivation, just facts and risks.\n\nMY PLAN:\n- Content: Book summaries (public domain classics + popular copyrighted books)\n- Length: 45 min to 3 hours per video\n- Language: Testing both Hindi and English\n- AI usage: ~90% (AI voice, AI-generated visuals, AI scripts — I only do manual script quality check and editing)\n- Monetization: AdSense + book affiliate links + sponsorships\n- Expansion: Spotify audio distribution if YouTube works\n\nANSWER THESE 5 THINGS:\n\n1. VIABILITY: Is the audiobook summary niche growing or saturated in 2025-2026? Give me realistic monthly search volume and competition level for keywords: \"book summary\", \"audiobook summary\", \"audiobook full\", \"[popular book] summary\" — check both Hindi and English.\n\n2. MONETIZATION RISK: With ~90% AI content (AI voice + AI visuals + AI script), what is the real risk of YouTube flagging this as \"reused content\" or \"inauthentic content\"? Are AI audiobook channels actually getting monetized right now? Note: I have the NexLev extension so I can verify any channel's monetization status myself — give me specific channels to check.\n\n3. RPM & REVENUE: What RPM range do audiobook/book summary channels typically earn? What's the difference between Hindi and English RPM in this specific niche?\n\n4. COPYRIGHT: Have any book summary channels been struck or taken down for summarizing copyrighted bestsellers like Atomic Habits, Rich Dad Poor Dad, etc.? What's the safe boundary — full narration vs summary vs commentary?\n\n5. HINDI vs ENGLISH: Based on current keyword data, which language has better growth potential for audiobook summaries? Consider: competition density, audience size, RPM, and number of existing channels.\n\nCHANNELS TO ANALYZE (these motivated me — check their performance, upload frequency, growth trajectory, and estimated RPM):\n- @SoulArcStudios\n- @LifeUpgrade27\n- @AudiobooksArc\n- @SwaroopSinghRajput\n- @Antidote_thechannel\n- @Elite_Audiobooks\n- @EnglishAvenuee — this one looks like standard AI-generated content but appears monetized. Why hasn't it been flagged?\n\nFor each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Line-by-Line Breakdown — Why Each Part Exists\n\n### Opening line\n> *\"I'm evaluating the YouTube audiobook/book summary niche before starting a channel.\"*\n\nTells the AI exactly what stage you're at — pre-launch research. Without this, it might give you growth tips instead of viability data.\n\n> *\"No fluff, no motivation, just facts and risks.\"*\n\nForces the AI to skip the \"Great question! Here's why this niche is amazing...\" sycophancy. Without this, you'll get 40% filler.\n\n---\n\n### MY PLAN section\n> *\"AI usage: ~90%\"*\n\nFixed the 90/95 contradiction. 90% is accurate — you're doing script QC manually, that's human editorial input.\n\n> *\"I only do manual script quality check and editing\"*\n\nThis is critical context. It tells the AI your exact level of human involvement, which directly affects the monetization risk answer.\n\n---\n\n### Question 1 — VIABILITY\n> *\"Give me realistic monthly search volume and competition level for keywords\"*\n\nThis is vidIQ's core strength — keyword data. By listing specific keywords, you prevent the AI from giving vague answers like \"it's a growing niche.\"\n\n> *\"check both Hindi and English\"*\n\nForces a direct comparison instead of a generic answer.\n\n---\n\n### Question 2 — MONETIZATION RISK\n> *\"Are AI audiobook channels actually getting monetized right now?\"*\n\nThis is the real question. Not \"can they be monetized theoretically\" but \"are they monetized TODAY.\"\n\n> *\"I have the NexLev extension so I can verify any channel's monetization status myself — give me specific channels to check.\"*\n\nThis is key. Instead of the AI claiming \"yes these channels are monetized\" (which could be hallucinated), you're telling it to give you names so YOU can verify with NexLev. Keeps the AI honest.\n\n---\n\n### Question 3 — RPM & REVENUE\n> *\"What's the difference between Hindi and English RPM in this specific niche?\"*\n\n\"In this specific niche\" is important. Generic Hindi vs English RPM data is useless — audiobook RPMs are different from gaming RPMs. Forces niche-specific data.\n\n---\n\n### Question 4 — COPYRIGHT\n> *\"Have any book summary channels been struck or taken down\"*\n\nReframed from \"what happens if I summarize copyrighted books\" (legal question vidIQ can't answer) to \"have channels been struck\" (observable fact vidIQ CAN answer).\n\n> *\"full narration vs summary vs commentary\"*\n\nThese are the three formats with very different risk levels. Full narration of a copyrighted book = high risk. Summary with commentary = transformative use = lower risk. This forces the AI to distinguish.\n\n---\n\n### Question 5 — HINDI vs ENGLISH\n> *\"Consider: competition density, audience size, RPM, and number of existing channels\"*\n\nWithout these specific criteria, the AI will just say \"English has more audience\" and stop. By listing 4 factors, you force a multi-dimensional answer.\n\n---\n\n### CHANNELS TO ANALYZE\n> *\"@SoulArcStudios, @LifeUpgrade27...\"*\n\nUsing @ handles instead of full URLs — vidIQ AI Coach recognizes handles better and can pull channel data directly.\n\n> *\"@EnglishAvenuee — this one looks like standard AI-generated content but appears monetized. Why hasn't it been flagged?\"*\n\nThis is your most important question buried in the channel list. By flagging it specifically, you force the AI to address the contradiction: \"if AI content gets flagged, why is THIS channel fine?\"\n\n> *\"For each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\"*\n\nWithout this line, the AI will give you vague qualitative descriptions. This forces a data table.\n\n---\n\n## What vidIQ CAN vs CANNOT Answer\n\n| Question | Can vidIQ Answer? | If Not, Who Can? |\n|----------|:-:|---|\n| Keyword search volume | ✅ Yes — core feature | — |\n| Channel stats (subs, views) | ✅ Yes | — |\n| RPM estimates | ⚠️ Rough estimates only | NexLev gives better RPM data |\n| Is a channel monetized? | ❌ No | **NexLev extension** — check yourself |\n| Copyright law / fair use | ❌ No | Ask me or consult a lawyer |\n| YouTube policy interpretation | ⚠️ General knowledge only | YouTube's official policy pages |\n| Will YouTube flag MY content? | ❌ No one can predict this | — |\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **After you get vidIQ's response:** Open each channel in your browser with NexLev active. Check monetization status, RPM, and revenue estimates yourself. Don't trust vidIQ's claims about whether a channel is monetized — verify with NexLev.\n\n---\n\n## What to Do After Pasting This Prompt\n\n1. **Paste the prompt** into vidIQ AI Coach\n2. **Read the response** — look for specific numbers, not vibes\n3. **Open each channel** with NexLev extension active → screenshot monetization status + RPM\n4. **Come back to me** with vidIQ's response + your NexLev screenshots\n5. I'll cross-check for hallucinations, do the copyright risk analysis vidIQ can't do, and give you the final verdict on whether to pursue this niche\n","Description":"Reviewed Priyanshu's audiobook niche prompt, fixed contradictions and weak points, created an optimized paste-ready version with line-by-line explanations.","Overwrite":false,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\41ca2d2f-d653-4452-b469-a994d6d476f7\\audiobook_niche_prompt_review.md","toolAction":"Creating prompt artifact","toolSummary":"Audiobook niche prompt review"}}]}
