ly, you force the AI to address the contradiction: \"if AI content gets flagged, why is THIS channel fine?\"\n151: \n152: > *\"For each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\"*\n153: \n154: Without this line, the AI will give you vague qualitative descriptions. This forces a data table.\n155: \n156: ---\n157: \n158: ## What vidIQ CAN vs CANNOT Answer\n159: \n160: | Question | Can vidIQ Answer? | If Not, Who Can? |\n161: |----------|:-:|---|\n162: | Keyword search volume | ✅ Yes — core feature | — |\n163: | Channel stats (subs, views) | ✅ Yes | — |\n164: | RPM estimates | ⚠️ Rough estimates only | NexLev gives better RPM data |\n165: | Is a channel monetized? | ❌ No | **NexLev extension** — check yourself |\n166: | Copyright law / fair use | ❌ No | Ask me or consult a lawyer |\n167: | YouTube policy interpretation | ⚠️ General knowledge only | YouTube's official policy pages |\n168: | Will YouTube flag MY content? | ❌ No one can predict this | — |\n169: \n170: > [!TIP]\n171: > **After you get vidIQ's response:** Open each channel in your browser with NexLev active. Check monetization status, RPM, and revenue estimates yourself. Don't trust vidIQ's claims about whether a channel is monetized — verify with NexLev.\n172: \n173: ---\n174: \n175: ## What to Do After Pasting This Prompt\n176: \n177: 1. **Paste the prompt** into vidIQ AI Coach\n178: 2. **Read the response** — look for specific numbers, not vibes\n179: 3. **Open each channel** with NexLev extension active → screenshot monetization status + RPM\n180: 4. **Come back to me** with vidIQ's response + your NexLev screenshots\n181: 5. I'll cross-check for hallucinations, do the copyright risk analysis vidIQ can't do, and give you the final verdict on whether to pursue this niche\n182: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to