a directly.\n\n> *\"@EnglishAvenuee — this is NOT AI-generated. It's human voiceover with simple captions on background images.\"*\n\nCorrects the AI's assumption before it happens. Without this clarification, vidIQ will assume it's AI content and give you a wrong risk analysis. By telling it upfront \"this is human-made but looks simple,\" you get an honest answer about whether AI replication of this format would survive.\n\n> *\"For each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\"*\n\nWithout this line, the AI will give you vague qualitative descriptions. This forces a data table.","StartLine":143,"TargetContent":"### CHANNELS TO ANALYZE\n> *\"@SoulArcStudios, @LifeUpgrade27...\"*\n\nUsing @ handles instead of full URLs — vidIQ AI Coach recognizes handles better and can pull channel data directly.\n\n> *\"@EnglishAvenuee — this one looks like standard AI-generated content but appears monetized. Why hasn't it been flagged?\"*\n\nThis is your most important question buried in the channel list. By flagging it specifically, you force the AI to address the contradiction: \"if AI content gets flagged, why is THIS channel fine?\"\n\n> *\"For each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\"*\n\nWithout this line, the AI will give you vague qualitative descriptions. This forces a data table.","TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\41ca2d2f-d653-4452-b469-a994d6d476f7\\audiobook_niche_prompt_review.md","toolAction":"Updating breakdown","toolSummary":"Line-by-line update"}}]}
