t RPM range do audiobook/book summary channels typically earn? What's the difference between Hindi and English RPM in this specific niche?\n49: \n50: 4. COPYRIGHT: Have any book summary channels been struck or taken down for summarizing copyrighted bestsellers like Atomic Habits, Rich Dad Poor Dad, etc.? What's the safe boundary — full narration vs summary vs commentary?\n51: \n52: 5. HINDI vs ENGLISH: Based on current keyword data, which language has better growth potential for audiobook summaries? Consider: competition density, audience size, RPM, and number of existing channels.\n53: \n54: 6. TOP CHANNELS: Give me the top 5 Hindi and top 5 English audiobook/book summary channels right now (outside of my list below). For each: subscribers, monthly views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM. I need this to judge if this niche is actually worth entering.\n55: \n56: 7. FORMAT REPLICABILITY: Look at @EnglishAvenuee — this channel uses a simple format: real human voiceover + captions on whiteboard/background images. Very minimal production. It's NOT AI-generated, it's human-made. Yet it earns extremely well. My question: Can I replicate this exact simple format using AI tools (AI voiceover instead of human, same caption-on-background style) and still get monetized without being flagged? What's the risk?\n57: \n58: CHANNELS TO ANALYZE (these motivated me — check their performance, upload frequency, growth trajectory, and estimated RPM):\n59: - @SoulArcStudios\n60: - @LifeUpgrade27\n61: - @AudiobooksArc\n62: - @SwaroopSinghRajput\n63: - @Antidote_thechannel\n64: - @Elite_Audiobooks\n65: - @EnglishAvenuee — this is NOT AI-generated. It's human voiceover with simple captions on background images. Very low production effort but high earnings. Analyze why this format works and whether I can replicate it with AI tools.\n66: \n67: For each channel: subscribers, total views, upload frequency, average views per video, and estimated RPM range.\n68: ```\n6