{"step_index":46,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T10:36:53Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-21T16:06:53+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-21T16:06:53+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/renu5/Downloads/priyanshu%20readme/knowledge/core_rules.md`\nTotal Lines: 61\nTotal Bytes: 2725\nShowing lines 1 to 61\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Core Rules: Session Persistence (Non-Negotiable)\n2: \n3: These rules apply to every session in this workspace.\n4: \n5: ## RULE 1: If it's not in the repo, it didn't happen\n6: - Every decision, fact about the business/clients/projects, preference stated, plan, draft, and learning gets written to a `.md` file in this repo.\n7: - Never answer \"I remember from earlier in the chat\". If it matters, it goes in a file.\n8: - Write in plain Markdown that a fresh agent with zero chat history could read and fully understand.\n9: \n10: ## RULE 2: Repo knowledge structure\n11: Keep this structure (create it if missing):\n12: - `/CONTEXT.md`: Master index.\n13: - `/knowledge/`: One file per topic. Topic file = the truth.\n14: - `/decisions.md`: Dated log: YYYY-MM-DD, decision, reason.\n15: - `/sessions/`: One file per session.\n16: - `/work/`: Actual deliverables (drafts, docs, code, assets).\n17: \n18: Session file template:\n19: ```markdown\n20: # <Date> <Topic>\n21: ## Goal\n22: ## What was done\n23: ## Decisions made (also copied to decisions.md)\n24: ## New knowledge (also merged into knowledge/ and CONTEXT.md)\n25: ## Open items / next steps\n26: ## Files changed\n27: ```\n28: Never delete old knowledge. If something becomes outdated, mark it \"SUPERSEDED YYYY-MM-DD by <file>\" and keep it.\n29: \n30: ## RULE 3: Session start (boot)\n31: At the start of every session, before doing any task